# Contribution attribution

- Use `Contributed-by: <Assistant or Tool> | <Complete Model or System>`
  commit trailers and exactly one visible `Sole author:` PR header; preserve
  `Co-Authored-By` trailers. Follow the sole-author rule from #284 and the
  [canonical policy](../../docs/contribution-attribution-policy.md).
- Do not add in-file tags. Keep historical tags until separately authorized cleanup.
- Attribution records acknowledge actual contributions only; they do not authenticate
  identity or replace approval, exact-SHA review, CI, security or merge gates.
- Work produced or materially authored by a provider remains attributed solely
  to that provider or those providers. The acting Director/Claude does not inherit
  authorship through delegation, routing, coordination, QA, review, acceptance,
  relay, merge eligibility evaluation, or merge execution; those activities
  create no code authorship, and no tag may imply inherited authorship.
- Before handoff, run `PYTHONPATH=src python scripts/check_contribution_tags.py
  --base <base-sha> --head <head-sha>` on the committed candidate.
